```

But Builder creates:
```perl
Chalk::IR::Node->new(op => 'Store')  # Builder creates this instead!
```

---

### 5. **What Would Need to Change**

To make Builder create polymorphic nodes consistently, you need to change 23 methods in Builder:

#### **Example Fix for Store:**

**Before (line 185):**
```perl
method build_store_node($var_name, $value_node, $control = undef) {
    my $ctrl = $control // $current_control // '__CONTROL_PLACEHOLDER__';
    my $value_ref = { op => 'NodeRef', node_id => $value_node->id };
    my $attributes = {
        name => $var_name,
        value => $value_ref
    };
    my $node_id = $self->next_node_id();
    my $store = Chalk::IR::Node->new(            # ← Generic
        id            => $node_id,
        op            => 'Store',
        inputs        => [$ctrl, $value_node->id],
        attributes    => $attributes,
    );
    $graph->add_node($store);
    $scope->define($var_name, $store->id);
    return $store;
}
```

**After:**
```perl
method build_store_node($var_name, $value_node, $control = undef) {
    my $ctrl = $control // $current_control // '__CONTROL_PLACEHOLDER__';
    my $node_id = $self->next_node_id();
    my $store = Chalk::IR::Node::Store->new(     # ← Polymorphic
        id            => $node_id,
        inputs        => [$ctrl, $value_node->id],
    );
    $graph->add_node($store);
    $scope->define($var_name, $store->id);
    return $store;
}
```

